@@ -76,6 +76,12 @@ Running the t2smap workflow
 
 This workflow uses multi-echo data to optimally combine data across echoes and
 to estimate T2* and S0 maps or time series.
+``t2smap`` accepts either 4D echo-specific time series or 3D echo-specific
+single-volume images, provided in ascending echo-time order. A single
+z-concatenated 3D or 4D file is also accepted. Single-volume inputs are treated
+as one-volume data for T2*/S0 estimation and T2*-based optimal combination.
+The ``--combmode paid`` option requires more than one volume because its SNR
+weights are estimated from temporal variance.
 To see which files are generated by this workflow, check out the workflow
 documentation: :py:func:`tedana.workflows.t2smap_workflow`.
 
